# P09.32 — Single inheritance of Rust polymorphic classes +
# `dynamic_cast` across the inheritance chain.
#
# The v1 capstone. Enables `pub class Dog : Animal { … }` syntax
# in the fork — derived classes embed the base subobject at
# offset 0, emit a combined vtable, chain typeinfo via
# `__si_class_type_info`, and get `dynamic_cast<Dog*>(animal*)`
# working for free via libc++abi.
#
# # Scope
#
# v1 covers:
#
# - Single inheritance only (one base per derived class).
# - Derived class MAY add new virtual methods (go into vtable
#   slots after base's).
# - Derived class MAY NOT override base virtuals. A method with
#   the same name as a base virtual emits as a new distinct
#   virtual, not as an override. Calls through a base pointer
#   therefore reach the base's implementation. **Override
#   support is deferred to v2.**
# - `dynamic_cast<Derived*>(base_ptr)` and
#   `dynamic_cast<Base*>(derived_ptr)` both work via libc++abi's
#   runtime typeinfo-chain walk.
#
# # What's new
#
# ## Attribute plumbing (`#[rustc_cxx_base]`)
#
# 7-file pattern (same as prior rustc_cxx_* attrs):
# - `rustc_span/src/symbol.rs` — new sym.
# - `rustc_feature/src/builtin_attrs.rs` — rustc_attr entry.
# - `rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs` — AttributeKind.
# - `rustc_hir/src/attrs/encode_cross_crate.rs` — `Yes`.
# - `rustc_passes/src/check_attr.rs` — allowlist.
# - `rustc_attr_parsing/src/attributes/codegen_attrs.rs` —
#   parser (`Target::Field`).
# - `rustc_attr_parsing/src/context.rs` — registered.
#
# ## Parser (`parse_cxx_class_item`)
#
# Accepts `class Name : Base { … }` syntax (C++-style
# inheritance header). When present, synthesizes a first field
# `__base: Base` carrying `#[rustc_cxx_base]`. The `__base`
# name is added to `sym::` so it's pre-interned. Users
# initialize it in ctors with the usual struct-literal syntax:
# `Self { __base: Base::new(…), other_field: … }`.
#
# ## Layout (`cxx_bridge::correct_layout`)
#
# `has_polymorphic_base(tcx, def)` — helper checking if the
# first field carries `#[rustc_cxx_base]`. When true, the
# polymorphic-shift pathway (P09.25) is skipped because the
# base subobject's first 8 bytes already ARE the vptr slot.
# Derived classes now report `sizeof(Base) + sizeof(extra_fields)`
# rather than re-adding a second vptr.
#
# ## Itanium mangler helpers (`rustc_symbol_mangling::itanium`)
#
# - `polymorphic_base_of_class(tcx, adt_did)` — returns
#   `Option<DefId>` of the base ADT if the class is derived.
# - `virtuals_on_chain(tcx, adt_did)` — recursive walk from
#   root to `adt_did` collecting virtuals in vtable order
#   (base first, derived last). Called by the vtable emitter.
# - `is_polymorphic_cpp_class` now returns true for derived
#   classes with no new virtuals of their own (they still
#   inherit the vtable slot from the base).
#
# ## Vtable / typeinfo emission (`rustc_codegen_llvm::cxx_vtable`)
#
# - `emit_vtable` uses `virtuals_on_chain` so derived classes
#   include base's slots first. Slot indices stay stable
#   between base and derived, which is what lets a
#   `static_cast<Animal*>(dog)` call Animal's virtuals at the
#   same slot index Animal's own vtable uses.
# - `emit_typeinfo` dispatches on
#   `polymorphic_base_of_class`:
#   - Root classes: 2-slot `__class_type_info` (as before).
#   - Derived: 3-slot `__si_class_type_info` — RTTI vtable
#     pointer (to `_ZTVN10__cxxabiv120__si_class_type_infoE`),
#     typeinfo name, and base's `_ZTI<Base>` pointer. The
#     third slot is what libc++abi's dynamic_cast walks to
#     determine inheritance chain membership.
#
# ## Ctor vptr init at return (`rustc_codegen_ssa::mir::block`)
#
# The tricky bit. P09.25 injects a vptr store at function
# entry. For derived classes, user code like
# `Self { __base: Base::new(…), other_field: … }` writes
# Base's bytes (including Base's vptr) into offset 0 of Self
# AFTER our entry-point injection — clobbering our derived
# vptr. Fix: also inject the store at each RETURN terminator
# in `codegen_return_terminator`. For derived classes this is
# the write that wins (it's last); for non-derived classes
# it's redundant with the entry injection but harmless.
#
# # Files
#
# Compiler (~180 LOC across 10 files):
#
# - `rustc_span/src/symbol.rs` — `__base`, `rustc_cxx_base` syms.
# - `rustc_feature/src/builtin_attrs.rs` — attr entry.
# - `rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs` — AttributeKind.
# - `rustc_hir/src/attrs/encode_cross_crate.rs` — Yes.
# - `rustc_passes/src/check_attr.rs` — allowlist.
# - `rustc_attr_parsing/src/attributes/codegen_attrs.rs` —
#   parser.
# - `rustc_attr_parsing/src/context.rs` — registration.
# - `rustc_parse/src/parser/item.rs` — `class Name : Base`
#   parsing, __base field synthesis.
# - `rustc_ty_utils/src/layout/cxx_bridge.rs` —
#   `has_polymorphic_base` + layout skip.
# - `rustc_symbol_mangling/src/itanium.rs` —
#   `polymorphic_base_of_class`, `virtuals_on_chain`,
#   updated `is_polymorphic_cpp_class`.
# - `rustc_codegen_llvm/src/cxx_vtable.rs` — emit_typeinfo
#   branches on base; emit_vtable uses chain walk.
# - `rustc_codegen_ssa/src/mir/block.rs` — inject vptr write
#   before return terminator.
#
# # Validation
#
# - `/tmp/p09-35-inherit/` — Dog inherits from Animal, C++
#   calls `d->legs()`, `d->noise()`, `d->bark()` via `Dog*`,
#   and `a->legs()`, `a->noise()` via upcast `Animal*`.
#   `legs=4 noise=7 bark=30 up_legs=4 up_noise=7 — OK
#   (inheritance), exit 0`.
# - `/tmp/p09-36-dyncast/` — `dynamic_cast<Dog*>` on an
#   `Animal*` that actually points at a Dog succeeds; on a
#   plain Animal returns nullptr. Exit 0.
# - `/tmp/p09-25-auto-vptr/` regression — same-crate
#   polymorphic (no inheritance) still passes.
# - `/tmp/p09-30-class-kw/` regression — class keyword still
#   passes.
# - `cargo test --workspace` → 235/0 preserved.
